efc83867230a26bbcd4a6c4cf644b69e154b452e
# ^ The AB-JChess commit the prod image runs (scripts/engine-assets.sh reads the
# first line; this comment is ignored).
#
# AB-JChess (https://github.com/lxsgx23/AB-JChess, GPL-3, by lxsgx23) is a jieqi
# engine with its own NNUE. efc83867 is release AB-JChess-20261031: a new engine
# built on jqe's code (MIT, Devin O'Keefe; THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES in its repo), with
# net abjchess-20261030 (0.6 MB, against v0.2d's 144 MB) and about 65x v0.2d's
# speed per node. Measured against jqe 331a6e61/it014, the jieqi champion from
# 10-21, at our live 4 s/move and 4 threads over 600 games: 306-67-227, 0.566,
# +46 Elo [+20, +73] (mistboard-engine lab/jieqi-match/jqe-vs-abj-20261031,
# commit c01c608). The pin before it was v0.2d (fe35d87c), which jqe had beaten
# by +67 over 150 pairs.
#
# Only the binary is built here. The net is NOT in our engines release: the
# author allowed site use (lxsgx23/AB-JChess#1, 2026-09-30) on the terms that we
# fetch it from his release and never re-host it, so railpack.json runs
# scripts/fetch-abjchess-net.sh, which downloads his AB-JChess-20261031 zip,
# checks the zip's and the net's sha256, loads the net and checks bench 43125.
# Moving this pin means re-reading his release for the matching net.
#
# Built with the source's own src/isa/build_tier.sh (g++, static, LTO) for
# x86-64-avx2 (engine-assets.sh ABJ_ARCH), not the shared sse41 target: its
# strength is the net, and the NNUE runs several times slower without AVX2.
# Prod web measured 2026-09-30: AMD EPYC 9655, avx2 bmi2 avx512 present.
#
# UCI differences from v0.2d the server relies on: no MultiPV option (it always
# reports one line; an unknown setoption prints an info string and is ignored),
# EvalFile loads print "EvalFile loaded", and `go perft` and `bench` remain.
